repository, with this notice.

Provenance and headers. Each vendored file keeps the header its source had when it was copied; none was edited to add or remove a copyright line.
  - pigbench (bench/evals) and cluster/ (bench/k8s): copied from PiG commit aea6c243e3 (the last commit touching those directories on the integration branch, 2026-10-11). Their files carry
    only `SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`; PiG's LICENSE at that commit reads "MIT License, Copyright Michael Kinsy". Published PiG releases up to 0.4.1 carry a Hewlett Packard
    Enterprise Development LP copyright line in LICENSE that the later tree no longer has.
  - bench/compare (buffon/mock/shapes.py and the streaming shapes): copied from PiG commit 22cc5639c4 of the bolt-bench branch. Those files carry
    `SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright Hewlett Packard Enterprise Development LP` and `SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`, kept as they are.
  Which copyright line applies to which file, and whether the code is relicensed, is the owner's decision (docs/DESIGN.md section 11, item 2).

KaTeX 0.19.0 (MIT, Copyright (c) 2013-2020 Khan Academy and other contributors) is vendored unchanged in buffon/dashboard/vendor/katex/ (katex.min.js, katex.min.css, the woff2 fonts
and its LICENSE): `buffon dashboard` runs it under Node to set formulas at build time, and the published site ships its CSS, fonts and LICENSE.

Pi-Bolt's own benchmark suite (MIT) is not vendored: `buffon external run` runs it from a checkout. Pi-Bolt's published Linux results (bench/results/2026-10-11-linux-x64-0.8.0, MIT, Copyright (c) 2025 Mario Zechner) are copied unchanged into `external/results/` with their provenance (docs/EXTERNAL.md). The durable-bench method is not used (no licence found).
